sw/ - the cgra command-line tool
================================

A UNIX-style front end over libcgra: read the .cgra configuration language,
resolve device profiles, compile named modes/pipelines into per-PE words, and
move vectors in and out through stdin/stdout so kernels compose in pipes.

Files
-----
    main.c        getopt_long parsing + every subcommand + vector I/O + shell
    bench_ref.h .c independent scalar benchmark references (no emulator/compiler execution)
    dsl.h dsl.c   the .cgra language: model, parser, config discovery
    compile.h .c  mode -> config words -> execution; adapters to libcgra's
                  matvec/scan/conv engines (length returns and CLI error text)

Layout
------
    config/       reference .cgra files (config/stdlib/ = bundled library)
    completions/  bash completion
    scripts/      CLI-driven pipelines (cgra-bench.sh)
    test/         assert.h unit tests for the DSL + compiler
    doc/          man pages (cgra.1, cgra.5) + texinfo manual (cgra.texi)

Options are parsed with getopt_long (they may appear anywhere; bare negative
numbers go after "--" or via --a/--b/stdin). `cgra shell` is an interactive
prompt with readline line-editing + history when readline is present (detected
by pkg-config), else it falls back to fgets.

Build (make -f sw.mk <target>)
------------------------------
    all                  build/cgra          (default; builds ../lib first)
    unit                 assert.h unit tests (DSL + compiler)
    smoke                CLI smoke tests against the sim: emulator
    test                 unit + smoke
    PROFILE=asan test    everything under AddressSanitizer + UBSan
    bench DEV=sim        stress-bench the whole stdlib (scripts/cgra-bench.sh)
    valgrind             unit tests under valgrind
    analyze              gcc -fanalyzer static analysis
    gprof|perf|callgrind profile the CLI driving the emulator (CPU-bound)
    doc                  makeinfo the texi manual + lint/render the man pages
    clean

Profiles (PROFILE=...): release (default, -O3 -DNDEBUG), debug, asan, ubsan,
gprof (-pg), perf (-O2 -g, frame pointers). The gprof/perf/callgrind targets
rebuild with the right instrumentation automatically.

Try it (no FPGA)
----------------
    build/cgra selftest
    build/cgra run add -d sim --a "1 2 3 4" --b "10 20 30 40"   # 11 22 33 44
    seq -20 20 | build/cgra run relu -d sim --json | jq '.result'

Docs
----
    man sw/doc/cgra.1      the command reference
    man sw/doc/cgra.5      the .cgra file format
    info sw/build/cgra     the full manual (make -f sw.mk info first)
Library API: libcgra(3) in lib/doc/.
